      "writtenOn": "2024-12-20T21:52:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003ethis seems like it could affect both performance and the visual representation of resources\n\nit can\u0027t affect visual representation as zlib is losless, and the performance impact is negligible, but I get your point.\n\nThe issue of having eng builds so different is that it makes no sense to use them locally, and one has to build userdebug if they ever want to profile anything - otherwise you rebuild the whole thing twice (to userdebug and back to eng) just for a single profiling session, which is annoying and also happens when you want to gather the data _right now_. So IMO the policy of having the builds _exactly the same_ is overly restrictive when eng build is so much slower than all the rest.\n\nI guess it will be just our team who can benefit from faster userdebug builds using the internal aapt2 tweaks. Thanks",
      "parentUuid": "309a127b_ad137056",
